  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INCREASING HEALTH WORKERS CAPACITY TO CONTRIBUTE TO THE REDUCTION OF MATERNAL, NEONATAL, INFANT AND CHILD MORTALITY THROUGH A NATIONAL TASK SHARING PR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing health workers capacity to contribute to the reduction of maternal, neonatal, infant and child mortality through a national task sharing program in 4 county hospitals in Grand Gedeh, River Gee, River cess and Sinoe. The program is an existing task-sharing in advanced obstetric care and advanced neonatal care which concentrates on the training of 8 senior nurses recruited from 4 rural counties (Grand Gedeh, River Cess, River Gee, and Sinoe) to become paediatric clinicians after 2 years.</narrative>
  </description>
